    a: "Advanced accounting questions test whether you can see through reported numbers to the economics. Book and tax rules differ, so companies carry deferred tax assets and liabilities. Leases sit on the balance sheet, but US GAAP and IFRS put their cost in different places, which moves EBITDA. Acquisitions create goodwill and intangibles; partial stakes bring the equity method and noncontrolling interest. Convertibles, preferred and PIK debt change interest, EPS and dilution. Two questions recur: is this a real, recurring cost, and are numerator and denominator on the same basis?",
