    example: "A [[$500M]] 5-year convertible pays [[1%]]; straight debt would cost [[6%]]. US GAAP interest is about $5M a year plus fee amortization. IFRS records a liability of about $394.7M (the present value of the payments at 6%) and $105.3M in equity; year 1 interest is about $23.7M, of which $5M is cash.",
    trap: "Older US filings show larger non-cash interest because the cash conversion model split many convertibles until ASU 2020-06 took effect, from 2022 for most public companies. Either way, dilution is counted with the if-converted method."
