    why: "The obligation (the projected benefit obligation, or PBO) is the present value of pensions employees have earned so far, including expected pay rises, discounted at high-quality corporate bond yields. Plan assets are carried at fair value. A defined contribution plan such as a 401(k) creates no such liability: the company's cost ends with each contribution. With a defined benefit plan the company bears the investment and longevity risk, which is why a deficit is treated like debt, although contribution timing is flexible within funding rules.",
